# Design System Rules

## Core principle
Reuse existing design-system tokens and components. Never hardcode hex colors, arbitrary pixel spacing, or one-off styles when an existing token/component already covers the case.

## Components
- Prefer shadcn primitives from `@/components/ui` for shared UI (buttons, inputs, dialogs, etc.) — do not hand-roll a duplicate of an existing primitive.
- Feature-specific UI lives in `src/features/<feature>/components/`. Promote to `@/components/shared/` only when reused by 2+ features.
- Do not hand-edit `@/components/ui` for a one-off usage — extend via `cva` variants, or override with `className` + `cn()`. Add new shadcn pieces with the CLI (`pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>`).
- Icons:
  - App/UI icons from the Figma Icons frame: import from `@/components/icons` (e.g. `IconHomeLine`, `IconSearchMd`). Color via `currentColor` + Tailwind `text-*`; size via `size` (default 20).
  - shadcn primitives may still use `lucide-react` where the CLI scaffolds them — prefer `@/components/icons` for product UI that must match the design system.
  - Site favicons / brand marks: raster assets under `assets/images/` (e.g. `favicon-*.png`) — not React SVG icons.
  - Do not inline raw SVG when an `@/components/icons` component already covers the case.

## Tokens (Tailwind v4 CSS-first)
All tokens live in `src/index.css` (`@theme inline` + `:root` / `.dark`). There is **no** `tailwind.config.*` and **no** `src/styles/tokens.css`.

Use the **mapped Tailwind utilities**, not raw `var(--…)` / hex in components:

| Concern | Source in `src/index.css` | Example utilities |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Figma palette | `--color-neutral-*`, `--color-teal-*`, `--color-red-*` | `bg-teal-700`, `text-neutral-500` |
| shadcn semantic roles | `--color-background`, `--color-primary`, … | `bg-background`, `text-primary`, `border-border` |
| Spacing (Figma `spacing-*`) | `--spacing-*` | `p-100`, `gap-200`, `mt-300` (not default Tailwind `p-4` / `p-[13px]`) |
| Radius (Figma `radius-*`) | `--radius-*` | `rounded-10`, `rounded-full` |
| Typography presets | `--text-preset-*` (+ line-height, letter-spacing) | `text-preset-1 font-bold`, `text-preset-3-semibold font-semibold` |
| Breakpoints | `--breakpoint-*` | `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:` |

- Prefer semantic roles (`bg-primary`) for app chrome; use palette primitives (`bg-teal-700`) when matching Figma literally.
- If a Figma value is missing, **add a token in `src/index.css` first** — do not hardcode `text-[#111827]` or `p-[13px]`.
- Merge classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` (or `cn` as used by shadcn components) — do not string-concatenate `className`.

## Layout & theming
- Match spacing patterns from sibling components before inventing new values.
- Desktop only for now — do not add mobile or responsive breakpoint styles unless asked.
- Theming: `.dark` class via `@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *))` in `src/index.css`. Do not introduce a second mechanism (e.g. `data-theme`).

## Files to reference before implementing UI
- `src/index.css` — source of truth for all design tokens.
- `src/stories/design-system/` — Storybook galleries for colors, typography, spacing, radius (`pnpm storybook`).
- `components.json` — shadcn aliases, style, and icon library.
- `src/components/ui/` — canonical shadcn primitives.
- `.cursor/rules/styling.mdc` — deeper Tailwind / shadcn styling conventions.

## When in doubt
- If a design requirement cannot be met with existing tokens/components, flag it to the user instead of silently inventing a one-off — propose adding a token or extending a `cva` variant.
